        "international": "Maps to CSTA data/networks, UNESCO communication and critical evaluation, ACARA digital systems. Use school-approved search tools.",
        "teach": "Read this out:\n“Data is facts we collect on purpose — favourite fruit, not your home address.”\n\nThen say it in your own words:\nYear 3 collect or present information for “What is data?”.\n\nWrite these words up and read the meanings:\ndata — Facts collected on purpose to answer a question.\ncollect — Gather facts carefully, without private details.\nrecord — Write the facts down so you do not lose them.\nchart — A picture of data, such as a bar chart, so you can compare.\nquestion — What you are trying to find out.\nevidence — Proof from your work, not a guess.\n\nTell them what “finished” looks like:\n1. Collect or show information for “What is data?” without private details\n2. Make a table, tally or chart someone else can read\n3. Write one sentence of what the information shows\n\nThis week is talk and paper first. Devices are optional.\n\nYou are teaching Year 3: What is data?. You do not need extra computing knowledge beyond this page.",
