    "teach": "Read this out:\n“If the path is red, turn. If not, go. That is a decision.”\n\nThen say it in your own words:\nYear 3 write a short program about “Decisions: if this, then that (intro)”.\n\nWrite these words up and read the meanings:\nif — A check: only do this if the condition is true.\nelse — What to do when the “if” is not true.\ncondition — The yes/no check a program makes, such as “score > 10”.\nchoice — Picking one path or another.\ntrue — The condition is yes.\nfalse — The condition is no.\n\nTell them what “finished” looks like:\n1. Build a short program that shows “Decisions: if this, then that (intro)”\n2. Run it and say what each main block does\n3. Change one thing, predict, then test\n\nAfter the talk task, open ByteBuddies if logins work. If they do not, stay on paper — that still counts as the lesson.\n\nYou are teaching Year 3: Decisions: if this, then that (intro). You do not need extra computing knowledge beyond this page.",
